Think:

key → value

Program:
server = {
    "hostname": "web01",
    "ip": "192.168.1.10",
    "os": "Ubuntu",
    "environment": "production"
}

Access:
print(server["hostname"])
print(server["ip"])

Output:
web01
192.168.1.10

This structure becomes extremely useful when working with:

JSON
APIs
AWS
Ansible
configuration data
server inventories
